  "summary": "The British and French offensive on the Somme in northern France opened on 1 July 1916 on a front of about 25 miles and was shut down by Haig on 18 November. The British Army lost 57,000 men on the first day, or 57,470 including missing with 19,240 killed per Military History Matters. The National Army Museum says it failed to secure a breakthrough.",
